    "title": "Design: lighter controls",
    "why": "Jason, 2026-11-19: \"the inputs being the same color as the bg is a little weird. maybe a slightly lighter color\"; the round action buttons blending in; \"the score should be more subtle, use the circle look like the other circles, keep status bar the same\"; the active chip \"a little too dark, softer brown. and not quotes\"; his screenshot of Browse local businesses (dark text on brown). (1) A token, --tv-field (white 55% into the vellum), and a zero-specificity base rule for text boxes, dropdowns and text areas; the pages' own field rules onto it. (2) The 30-34px round action buttons rest in --tv-field with their brown ring (CLAUDE.md: rest cream with a brown ring). (3) The score ring: the field fill and a 1px brown ring like the others, its coloured arc unchanged, the number quieter. (4) Get Local's active chip: a softer brown (umber 40% into taupe), the search words without quote marks. (5) White text on brand brown for Browse local businesses (hub) and the listing's event button: 3b-2 had left dark text on them.",
